enchilada: WLFW request timeout compares signed elapsed time

wlfw_poll() gets the time t read at the top of the watch pass; a request sent later in the same pass has sent_at > t, so the unsigned t - sent_at wrapped and the request 'timed out' at once (boot45: ind_register 'no response in 10000 ms' 0 ms after sending, then the reply arrived as unexpected). Signed difference.

--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_mss.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_mss.c
@@ -3240,7 +3240,8 @@
 static bool
 wlfw_poll(unsigned t, bool end)
 {
-	if (wl.on && wl.pending && t - wl.sent_at > WLFW_TIMEOUT_MS) {
+	/* 0283: t is read before a request sent in the same pass: signed, or t - sent_at wraps to "timed out" */
+	if (wl.on && wl.pending && (int)(t - wl.sent_at) > (int)WLFW_TIMEOUT_MS) {
 		printf("SWEET WLFW: no response to %#x (%s) in %u ms\n", wl.pending, wl.step, WLFW_TIMEOUT_MS);
 		wl.pending = 0;
 		if (!wl.off_sent) {
